sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer App
    participant API as Node.js API
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL
    participant WS as Realtime Gateway
    participant D as Dispatcher Dashboard
    participant DR as Driver App
    participant N as Notification Worker
    participant WA as WhatsApp/Email Provider

    C->>API: Create booking draft
    API->>API: Validate request and recalculate fare
    API->>DB: Insert booking(status=pending_payment)
    DB-->>API: ticketId and booking record
    API-->>C: Draft booking + advance amount

    C->>API: Create Razorpay order
    API->>DB: Read persisted advance amount
    API-->>C: Razorpay order details
    C->>API: Payment provider webhook
    API->>API: Verify signature and event idempotency
    API->>DB: Atomic payment + booking transition
    DB-->>API: booking(status=paid_confirmed)
    API->>WS: Publish booking.paid_confirmed
    WS-->>D: New paid booking event
    API->>N: Queue payment confirmation
    N->>WA: Send customer confirmation

    D->>API: Request dispatch bookings
    API->>DB: Query paid bookings and available drivers
    DB-->>API: Dispatch candidates
    API-->>D: Dispatch queue

    D->>API: Assign driver and vehicle
    API->>DB: Transaction: validate availability and assign
    DB-->>API: booking(status=driver_assigned)
    API->>WS: Publish booking.driver_assigned
    WS-->>C: Driver assignment update
    WS-->>DR: New trip assignment
    API->>N: Queue assignment notifications
    N->>WA: Notify customer and driver

    DR->>API: Accept assignment
    API->>DB: Record driver acknowledgement
    API->>WS: Publish driver.assignment_acknowledged
    WS-->>D: Driver accepted trip

    Note over API,DB: Every state change is persisted before broadcast.
    Note over WS,C: Client treats events as hints and refreshes authoritative state via REST when needed.
